  {
   "user": "Benjamin Isaac",
   "message": "Question: What should be done about the 9 tons of lead explosives which are set to be detonated on Monday in Iowa? No wrong answers.",
   "timestamp": "2026-11-21T05:25:44.384000+00:00",
   "channel": "general",
   "channel_id": "discord:1344300408893345866",
   "thread": null,
   "thread_id": null,
   "reply_to": null,
   "id": "discord:1573570087523197009",
   "user_id": "discord:1004926447313498122",
   "is_bot": false,
   "url": "https://discord.com/channels/1344300408893345863/1344300408893345866/1573570087523197009",
   "attachments": [],
   "platform": "discord",
   "server": "ORI 1.0",
   "server_id": "discord:1344300408893345863"
  },
  {
   "user": "Benjamin Isaac",
   "message": "Welp, looks like they delayed it until Monday. Now we have a bad situation which they appeared to be trying in a controlled way before freezing weather makes it more unpredictable, so it could blow without people having a chance to get out of the way. https://www.iowapublicradio.org/ipr-news/2026-11-20/justice-department-oppose-block-iowa-army-detonation Like not doing controlled burn fires, but that makes the wildfires far worse. This is a risk of a one-time Big Event which hasn't happened yet, though. More ORI-relevant, though, is the fact that if someone could order a purposeful detonation which prevents a far worse event which never happens, the person who orders it is the villain, even though they likely prevented far worse stuff.\n\nAnd even more meme-relevant: it's possible the amount of press will result in more money which can be used to further reduce the plume (it's already happening in a concrete bunker with 2-story wet sandbags surrounding it).",
   "timestamp": "2026-11-21T06:29:53.196000+00:00",
